The Omit story, finished — and the scene's hover actions, born. A writer cannot omit a scene. The Navigator's scene rows get hover actions: Omit Scene on a live scene, Restore Scene on an omitted one (trailing edge, secondary color, SF Symbols), architected so Lock Scene and Scene Status slot in later — no greyed placeholders. Parity is mandatory: the same two commands as a right-click context menu on the scene heading in the text, and a menu bar item (Production menu if it exists; otherwise Format) that enables/disables with the caret's position. Done means: Omit with the caret anywhere in a scene collapses it to the card as real model state (Omission over the scene's elements); Restore is the reverse from the Navigator row, the card's context menu, or the menu bar; ⌘Z reverses omit/restore named "Undo Omit Scene"; page numbers and count exclude the cut body; FDX round-trips through the engine splice; Fountain documents either disable the command with a clear reason or warn; VoiceOver announces the action and result; no regression to the chevron, fade, caret anchoring, Navigator strike, both layouts, light and dark. Proof: EDraftCore and EDraftMacSurface suites green with new failing-before tests, macOS Debug build succeeds, measured before/after on a real FDX (omit → save → reopen; restore → save → reopen). Budget: EditorState/Omissions (EDraftCore), StoryPanel (EDraftUI), ScriptMenus/MainMenu, ScriptSurface or its context-menu path, tests in both packages. Deny the xcscheme, mcp.log, the root PNGs and the in-progress src/ help files. No commit until I say so.